  "releaseNotes": "Throw if model/factory not registered:\n      - Change GetModelI to return a non-nullable T and throw InvalidOperationException when no instance is registered (updates XML docs accordingly).\n      - Also adjust the factory getter to call the factory delegate directly and throw if no factory is registered.\n      - This enforces presence of registered models/factories instead of returning null and provides clearer error messages (includes the type full name in the exception).\n      - Files modified: Lucifer.cs, LuciferModel.cs.",
